  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Kazo OS 3.3.4, changes for app developers:\n- KazoAppPackages.InstallAsync reports its progress. A new overload InstallAsync(source, scope, IProgress<KazoPackageInstallProgress>?, cancellationToken) reports each KazoPackageInstallStage (Preparing, Downloading with BytesReceived and TotalBytes, Verifying, AwaitingApproval, Installing). The existing overload is unchanged; IAppManagementGateway gets a matching member with a default body. A cref to KazoAppPackages.InstallAsync without parameters is now ambiguous: name the overload.\n- A Craft app's exports reach its window as copies. A Craft app that exports through a browser download link (an <a download> on a blob: address, as PdfCraft does) no longer sends the file to the real computer's Downloads folder: when the window subscribes to the new CraftFrame.Exporting event, the Kazo.Os.AppSdk.Craft module takes the file and the window saves it as a copy through the OS save dialog (DocumentSession.DecideCopy). A window that does not subscribe keeps the browser download.\nRelease notes: https://github.com/Kazo-ca/Os/releases/tag/v3.3.4",
